171753.122: [17:17:53]
171753.122: [17:17:53]       The newest version of Nmap can be obtained from https://nmap.org. The newest version of this man page is available at https://nmap.org/book/man.html.  It is also included as a chapter of Nmap Network Scanning: The Official Nmap
171753.123: [17:17:53]       Project Guide to Network Discovery and Security Scanning (see https://nmap.org/book/).
171753.123: [17:17:53]
171753.123: [17:17:53]OPTIONS SUMMARY
171753.123: [17:17:53]       This options summary is printed when Nmap is run with no arguments, and the latest version is always available at https://svn.nmap.org/nmap/docs/nmap.usage.txt. It helps people remember the most common options, but is no substitute
171753.123: [17:17:53]       for the in-depth documentation in the rest of this manual. Some obscure options aren't even included here.
171753.123: [17:17:53]
171753.123: [17:17:53]           Nmap 7.70SVN ( https://nmap.org )
171753.123: [17:17:53]           Usage: nmap [Scan Type(s)] [Options] {target specification}
171753.123: [17:17:53]           TARGET SPECIFICATION:
171753.123: [17:17:53]             Can pass hostnames, IP addresses, networks, etc.
171753.123: [17:17:53]             Ex: scanme.nmap.org, microsoft.com/24, 192.168.0.1; 10.0.0-255.1-254
171753.124: [17:17:53]             -iL <inputfilename>: Input from list of hosts/networks
172311.096: [17:23:11]             -iR <num hosts>: Choose random targets
172311.139: [17:23:11]             --exclude <host1[,host2][,host3],...>: Exclude hosts/networks
172311.151: [17:23:11]             --excludefile <exclude_file>: Exclude list from file
172311.180: [17:23:11]           HOST DISCOVERY:
172311.214: [17:23:11]             -sL: List Scan - simply list targets to scan
172311.260: [17:23:11]             -sn: Ping Scan - disable port scan
172311.314: [17:23:11]             -Pn: Treat all hosts as online -- skip host discovery
172311.336: [17:23:11]             -PS/PA/PU/PY[portlist]: TCP SYN/ACK, UDP or SCTP discovery to given ports
172311.363: [17:23:11]             -PE/PP/PM: ICMP echo, timestamp, and netmask request discovery probes
172311.390: [17:23:11]             -PO[protocol list]: IP Protocol Ping
172311.435: [17:23:11]             -n/-R: Never do DNS resolution/Always resolve [default: sometimes]
172311.462: [17:23:11]             --dns-servers <serv1[,serv2],...>: Specify custom DNS servers
172311.532: [17:23:11]             --system-dns: Use OS's DNS resolver
172311.619: [17:23:11]             --traceroute: Trace hop path to each host
172311.643: [17:23:11]           SCAN TECHNIQUES:
172311.661: [17:23:11]             -sS/sT/sA/sW/sM: TCP SYN/Connect()/ACK/Window/Maimon scans
172311.686: [17:23:11]             -sU: UDP Scan
172311.734: [17:23:11]             -sN/sF/sX: TCP Null, FIN, and Xmas scans
172311.788: [17:23:11]             --scanflags <flags>: Customize TCP scan flags
172311.966: [17:23:11]             -sI <zombie host[:probeport]>: Idle scan
172312.176: [17:23:12]             -sY/sZ: SCTP INIT/COOKIE-ECHO scans
172312.205: [17:23:12]             -sO: IP protocol scan
172312.229: [17:23:12]             -b <FTP relay host>: FTP bounce scan
172312.255: [17:23:12]           PORT SPECIFICATION AND SCAN ORDER:
172312.312: [17:23:12]             -p <port ranges>: Only scan specified ports
172312.346: [17:23:12]               Ex: -p22; -p1-65535; -p U:53,111,137,T:21-25,80,139,8080,S:9
172312.434: [17:23:12]             --exclude-ports <port ranges>: Exclude the specified ports from scanning
172312.492: [17:23:12]             -F: Fast mode - Scan fewer ports than the default scan
172312.557: [17:23:12]             -r: Scan ports consecutively - don't randomize
172312.617: [17:23:12]             --top-ports <number>: Scan <number> most common ports
172314.072: [17:23:14]             --port-ratio <ratio>: Scan ports more common than <ratio>
172314.454: [17:23:14]           SERVICE/VERSION DETECTION:
172314.722: [17:23:14]             -sV: Probe open ports to determine service/version info
172316.711: [17:23:16]             --version-intensity <level>: Set from 0 (light) to 9 (try all probes)
172316.939: [17:23:16]             --version-light: Limit to most likely probes (intensity 2)
172317.582: [17:23:17]             --version-all: Try every single probe (intensity 9)
172317.779: [17:23:17]             --version-trace: Show detailed version scan activity (for debugging)
172318.034: [17:23:18]           SCRIPT SCAN:
172318.230: [17:23:18]             -sC: equivalent to --script=default
172318.291: [17:23:18]             --script=<Lua scripts>: <Lua scripts> is a comma separated list of
172318.340: [17:23:18]                      directories, script-files or script-categories
172318.390: [17:23:18]             --script-args=<n1=v1,[n2=v2,...]>: provide arguments to scripts
172318.421: [17:23:18]             --script-args-file=filename: provide NSE script args in a file
172318.450: [17:23:18]             --script-trace: Show all data sent and received
172318.491: [17:23:18]             --script-updatedb: Update the script database.
172318.524: [17:23:18]             --script-help=<Lua scripts>: Show help about scripts.
172318.584: [17:23:18]                      <Lua scripts> is a comma-separated list of script-files or
172318.642: [17:23:18]                      script-categories.
172319.069: [17:23:19]           OS DETECTION:
172319.558: [17:23:19]             -O: Enable OS detection
172319.843: [17:23:19]             --osscan-limit: Limit OS detection to promising targets
172320.056: [17:23:20]             --osscan-guess: Guess OS more aggressively
172320.269: [17:23:20]           TIMING AND PERFORMANCE:
172320.438: [17:23:20]             Options which take <time> are in seconds, or append 'ms' (milliseconds),
172321.365: [17:23:21]             's' (seconds), 'm' (minutes), or 'h' (hours) to the value (e.g. 30m).
172321.576: [17:23:21]             -T<0-5>: Set timing template (higher is faster)
172321.805: [17:23:21]             --min-hostgroup/max-hostgroup <size>: Parallel host scan group sizes
172321.901: [17:23:21]             --min-parallelism/max-parallelism <numprobes>: Probe parallelization
172322.156: [17:23:22]             --min-rtt-timeout/max-rtt-timeout/initial-rtt-timeout <time>: Specifies
172324.336: [17:23:24]                 probe round trip time.
172325.650: [17:23:25]             --max-retries <tries>: Caps number of port scan probe retransmissions.
172326.248: [17:23:26]             --host-timeout <time>: Give up on target after this long
172326.448: [17:23:26]             --scan-delay/--max-scan-delay <time>: Adjust delay between probes
172327.050: [17:23:27]             --min-rate <number>: Send packets no slower than <number> per second
172327.301: [17:23:27]             --max-rate <number>: Send packets no faster than <number> per second
172327.513: [17:23:27]           FIREWALL/IDS EVASION AND SPOOFING:
172329.711: [17:23:29]             -f; --mtu <val>: fragment packets (optionally w/given MTU)
172329.904: [17:23:29]             -D <decoy1,decoy2[,ME],...>: Cloak a scan with decoys
172329.949: [17:23:29]             -S <IP_Address>: Spoof source address
172330.008: [17:23:30]             -e <iface>: Use specified interface
172330.048: [17:23:30]             -g/--source-port <portnum>: Use given port number
172330.068: [17:23:30]             --proxies <url1,[url2],...>: Relay connections through HTTP/SOCKS4 proxies
172330.095: [17:23:30]             --data <hex string>: Append a custom payload to sent packets
172330.115: [17:23:30]             --data-string <string>: Append a custom ASCII string to sent packets
172330.135: [17:23:30]             --data-length <num>: Append random data to sent packets
172330.152: [17:23:30]             --ip-options <options>: Send packets with specified ip options
172330.178: [17:23:30]             --ttl <val>: Set IP time-to-live field
172330.204: [17:23:30]             --spoof-mac <mac address/prefix/vendor name>: Spoof your MAC address
172330.231: [17:23:30]             --badsum: Send packets with a bogus TCP/UDP/SCTP checksum
172330.276: [17:23:30]           OUTPUT:
172330.308: [17:23:30]             -oN/-oX/-oS/-oG <file>: Output scan in normal, XML, s|<rIpt kIddi3,
172330.343: [17:23:30]                and Grepable format, respectively, to the given filename.
172330.392: [17:23:30]             -oA <basename>: Output in the three major formats at once
172330.464: [17:23:30]             -v: Increase verbosity level (use -vv or more for greater effect)
172330.582: [17:23:30]             -d: Increase debugging level (use -dd or more for greater effect)
172330.769: [17:23:30]             --reason: Display the reason a port is in a particular state
172331.085: [17:23:31]             --open: Only show open (or possibly open) ports
172331.122: [17:23:31]             --packet-trace: Show all packets sent and received
172331.151: [17:23:31]             --iflist: Print host interfaces and routes (for debugging)
172331.161: [17:23:31]             --append-output: Append to rather than clobber specified output files
172331.182: [17:23:31]             --resume <filename>: Resume an aborted scan
172331.183: [17:23:31]             --stylesheet <path/URL>: XSL stylesheet to transform XML output to HTML
172331.205: [17:23:31]             --webxml: Reference stylesheet from Nmap.Org for more portable XML
